---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const root=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout title="HealthQualify Local Edition" description="A free offline-first local qualification dashboard. No mandatory cloud account, paid API token or LLM." active="local">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="live-dot"></span> YOUR MACHINE · YOUR EVIDENCE</div><h1>Local by design.<br/><em>Free by default.</em></h1><p class="lead">Create a local administrator, run a guided synthetic qualification, inspect evidence and launch advisory investigators—all without purchasing an AI API key.</p><div class="cta-row"><a class="button primary" href={root+'docs/LOCAL_EDITION_V08/'}>Installation guide ↗</a><a class="button ghost" href="https://github.com/Tec-Wel/HealthQualify">View source →</a></div></div></section>
<section class="section light"><div class="container local-split"><div><span class="kicker">GET STARTED</span><h2>One local workspace.<br/>No accounts to buy.</h2><p>From a checked-out repository with Python 3.10+, start the Local Edition. Its guided demo intentionally contains five seeded failures. The server binds to loopback and is not suitable for exposed hospital deployments.</p><div class="pill-list"><span>Windows</span><span>macOS</span><span>Linux</span><span>Offline core</span></div></div><div class="terminal"><div class="terminal-top">LOCAL TERMINAL</div><pre><code>git clone https://github.com/Tec-Wel/HealthQualify.git
cd HealthQualify
python -m healthqualify.local_edition_v08

<span class="terminal-dim"># Optional, installed separately:</span>
ollama pull qwen3:8b
python -m healthqualify.local_edition_v08 --allow-local-qwen</code></pre></div></div></section>
<section class="section pale"><div class="container compact"><span class="kicker">SAFETY BOUNDARY</span><h2>Human review stays in control.</h2><p>Draft demonstrations, scoped agent observations and reviewer acknowledgments do not constitute Part 11 electronic signatures, FDA authorization or a qualified regulated release.</p><a class="text-link" href={root+'docs/disclaimer-policy/'}>Read safety and regulatory disclaimer ↗</a></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
